 #     container's logs, sampling defaults and topology as its own.
+#   url_names_this_host URL
+#     exit 0 when URL's host IS this machine (loopback, or an address
+#     `hostname -I` reports), 1 when it names another machine or resolves to
+#     nothing. The same rule, asked without a mapping: it says WHY no container
+#     matched — the URL points elsewhere (worth saying) or a local port simply
+#     has none published (the endpoint is down) (#1584 follow-up).
